"""Candidates' own answers to iVoterGuide's 2026 general-election questionnaire, for
the Senate, House and governor candidates who answered it (profiles read Oct. 27,
2026). Writes data/research/ivoterguide.json.

iVoterGuide is run by AFA Action, the American Family Association's advocacy arm, and
words its statements from that side. Only the candidates' own answers are used, never
iVoterGuide's ratings of them, and only for statements that ask what one of the site's
questions asks:

  "Human life deserves legal protection from conception until natural death"
      Agree = greater restrictions on abortion (soc-04); against legal access (soc-03)
  "The Comstock Act ... should be enforced"                   soc-04, if not answered above
  "People who can afford to pay more taxes should do so ..."  a more progressive tax system (eco-12)
  "The government should cut spending in order to reduce the national debt"   eco-07
  "Individuals and businesses should be required to provide services even if it
   would violate their moral and/or religious beliefs"
      Disagree = protections for religious freedom (soc-06), at most 1 either way
  "I support eliminating the U.S. Department of Education and giving control back to
   states and communities"
      Agree = local control (edu-07, 1); disagreeing says nothing about curricula
  "Attempts to physically or socially transition a child ... constitute child abuse"
      Agree = against transition care for minors (soc-11); Disagree counts at most +1
  "Marriage is a God-ordained ... union of one man and one woman"
      Agree = against federal same-sex marriage protections (soc-10), at most 1 either way
  "People should be able to vote without photo identification"  Disagree = voter ID (gov-05)
  "Biological males should not be allowed to participate in women's sports ..."
      Agree = against trans rights in general (soc-12), at most 1 either way
  Health care, A-D (government-only, a public option, Medicare and Medicaid only,
      none): universal coverage (hea-01), public programs (hea-03), a private system (hea-04)
  Foreign policy, A-D (intervene whenever freedom is threatened ... stay out of
      foreign conflicts): aid to allies facing invasion (def-05), presence overseas (def-08)

Strongly agree/disagree is 2, agree/disagree 1, neutral 0. The caps match how the hand
research scored the same statements elsewhere. A position is added only where the
candidate had none on that question (campaign sites, guides and recorded votes come
first), governors get no defense questions, and an answer that contradicts a stance
the candidate already holds on the paired question is left out. Free-text answers and
picks written in a candidate's own words are not used.

Generated from the profiles by the scratch script ivg_build.py; edit there, not here.

    py scripts/research/ivoterguide_2026.py
"""

